WEBVTT

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.740
You appear to be having fun, my lord.

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:15.520
Yes. Journeys are splendid things.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:17.570
They rouse the heart.

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:19.990
I went to all the trouble of readying the horses.

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:23.460
There are things you cannot see from horseback.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:24.870
That you can't see?

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:28.790
The lands I will conquer.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:35.220
You will never broaden your horizons by 
only looking down from the castle.

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:37.410
You're amazing, my lord!

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:39.240
This isn't the time for happiness!

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:42.500
Even as we speak, they may be

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:45.310
raising their armies against us.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:47.900
But Masamune-san said...

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:51.900
Mouri, Ootomo, and Chousokabe of Saigoku

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:55.900
possess the remaining three pieces of armor.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:59.080
Each of them is a valiant warrior,

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:01.950
but has little interest in conquest.

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:04.420
Depending upon your negotiating skill,

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:06.260
they may simply hand over the armor.

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:08.040
That's what she said!

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:09.280
But...

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:10.960
Don't worry, Mitsuhide.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:16.250
It would be rude to go, 
without allowing them time to greet us.

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:17.510
And...

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:26.920
If I can't get my hands on the armor,

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:30.310
it just means that I wasn't worthy of it.

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:31.930
OK!

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:34.190
Then let's go!

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:37.590
Akerin...

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:39.910
How far to Saigoku?

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:41.740
A long way.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:42.990
Don't be stupid!

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:46.830
But we've been walking all day.

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:49.360
You're already giving up?

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:50.600
Useless.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:51.730
No.

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:54.340
My lord and Akerin are too tough.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:58.610
Living in this era might be hard, after all.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:38.900
<b>Episode 8</b>

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:38.900
<b>Fever Maiden</b>

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:48.980
Be of good cheer, Hideyoshi!

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.940
We shall rest in this town.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:52.960
<b>Dumplings</b>

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:55.150
Really?

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:56.730
All right!

00:03:58.640 --> 00:03:59.970
Excuse me!

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:01.630
Dumplings and tea for three!

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:03.600
Right away!

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:05.870
Oh, my. You're samurai.

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:06.930
Where are you from?

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:08.320
Yes, we are...

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:09.010
Indeed!

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:11.570
Listen to my words, and be amazed.

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:16.980
For before you stands the 
great Oda Nobunaga-sama of Owari!

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:19.400
Nobunaga?

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:20.570
Nobunaga?

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:21.360
Nobunaga?

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:24.660
She definitely just said Nobunaga.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:29.300
Isn't this how they shouldn't react?

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:35.250
Samurai, are you really Oda Nobunaga-sama?

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:38.380
Indeed, I am Oda Nobunaga.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:39.910
N-Nobunaga...

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:41.220
The cannibal of Owari!

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:42.320
Hide the children!

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:43.700
She'll eat them!

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:58.210
They all left.

00:04:58.210 --> 00:04:59.840
What is this?

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:00.980
You, girl!

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:07.100
What is the meaning of this?

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:09.660
Why did they all hide when 
they heard that I am Nobunaga?

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:12.630
Th-There's a rumor that Oda Nobunaga of Owari

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:15.410
takes her people's babies and devours them!

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:16.580
The hell?

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:18.120
Don't be stupid!

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:21.590
Who would spread such a ridiculous rumor?

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:24.760
A samurai called Akechi Mitsuhide.

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:28.300
Everyone on the road, from here to Saigoku,

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:30.880
is talking about the evil Nobunaga-sama!

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:34.030
Mitsuhide...

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:37.810
What is this?

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:39.840
Th-Th-This is a misunderstanding!

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:41.410
Some kind of mistake...

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:46.370
Everyone, spread rumors,

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:47.640
from here to Saigoku.

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:48.390
Yes, ma'am.

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:50.810
Nobunaga-sama is not only strong,

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:52.870
but kind, as well.

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:56.510
When Nobunaga-sama comes, the Owari people

00:05:56.510 --> 00:06:00.460
ask her to pat their children and babies' heads.

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:01.600
Yes, ma'am.

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:03.750
And don't forget to tell them

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:06.360
that it was Mitsuhide who spread the rumors.

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:07.170
Yes, ma'am!

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:21.710
I hear Nobunaga-sama is also kind 
to children and infants.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:26.220
The people all ask her to pat their babies.

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:29.040
That's what Akechi Mitsuhide-sama said.

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:30.910
I see...

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:33.320
When Nobunaga-sama comes,

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:39.030
the people all rush to offer her 
their children, Akechi Mitsuhide-sama.

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:42.040
Oh, my... I see.

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:48.570
Akechi Mitsuhide-sama says that
the samurai that goes by Nobunaga

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:51.100
kidnaps her people's children...

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:55.560
How terrifying!

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:57.980
I demand meat!

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:02.070
The soft meat of children!

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:05.840
Akechi Mitsuhide-sama says that Oda Nobunaga

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:09.860
is a demon in human form that 
devours children and infants!

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:11.830
How horrible.

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:14.480
Are we to be visited by such a monster?

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:19.410
Akechi Mitsuhide-sama says that Oda Nobuaga of Owari

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:22.460
is the most cruel, tyrannical, 
lascivious, supercilious,

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:24.960
and topological lord in all the land!

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:26.770
Oh, man...

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:31.600
Mitsuhide, you...

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:34.990
Why was my name the only thing they got right?

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:51.150
So the Oda kid has left?

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:54.310
Yes, she's heading west.

00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:55.080
West?

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:57.060
Then where is she going?

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:58.310
I don't know.

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:00.540
You don't know?

00:08:01.490 --> 00:08:06.690
That's your job, Hanzou!

00:08:07.160 --> 00:08:09.210
I'm terribly sorry!

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:10.740
You fool!

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:15.800
I'm terribly sorry, my lord...

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:17.620
Thanks to that rumor,

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:20.640
we'll have to think twice before we 
stop at any of the towns up ahead.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:22.450
It can't be helped.

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:24.310
Let's follow this animal trail.

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.850
I'm hungry...

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:41.580
My lord, I can't go on!

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:44.110
You're right.

00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:45.260
Let's eat.

00:08:45.260 --> 00:08:46.060
Yes, my lord.

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:47.840
A packed lunch!

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:51.530
Um... This...

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:54.840
Watch.

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:01.470
It's hoshiii.

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:03.450
Chew it before you swallow.

00:09:03.450 --> 00:09:05.670
There's niboshi and miso, too.

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:06.980
This is a feast.

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:11.070
<b>NIBOSHI 
Niboshi are small, boiled, and dried fish. 
Most often Japanese anchovies, but Japanese sardines, 
round herring, silver-stripe round herring, horse mackerel, 
mackerel, and flying fish are also used. 
It is known by many other names, including iriko, jako, and dashijako.</b>

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:12.440
<b>HOSHII 
Hoshii is rice that has been dried after cooking. 
As the rice is merely bleached lightly in water, then left to sun dry, 
it was once used to preserve overcooked rice. 
There are also rations and preserved foods 
called hoshi or hoshii.</b>

00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:13.820
<b>MISO 
Miso is a traditional Japanese dish, 
made by fermenting crops, primarily soybeans.</b>

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:20.420
Tuna onigiri from the convenience store,

00:09:20.420 --> 00:09:21.830
salisbury steak at a restaurant...

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:37.720
My lord... Is this really the right way?

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:39.780
Don't worry.

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:43.220
Once we're over this cliff, we're nearly at the road.

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:53.030
Looks like we're lost.

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:56.490
Then we're totally stranded!

00:09:56.960 --> 00:09:58.860
It's fine.

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:01.650
We're going the right way, and it's still early.

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:03.240
What do you think, Mitsuhide?

00:10:03.650 --> 00:10:07.120
Two more mountains, 
and I think we'll reach a village.

00:10:07.770 --> 00:10:09.630
Two more?

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:13.160
If we rest, the sun will go down!

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:14.210
But...

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:17.390
If you don't want to end up wolf food, 
you have to walk!

00:10:18.210 --> 00:10:19.340
Wolves?

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:29.140
It looks like we've reached the path.

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:30.610
Let's go.

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:31.400
Yes.

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:37.460
There's no map, no cell phone, or GPS.

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:39.740
If I were alone...

00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:45.210
No! No!

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:46.430
I don't want that to happen!

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:48.010
What are you doing, Hideyoshi?

00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:50.190
We'll leave you behind! Hurry!

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:53.320
Please wait!

00:10:58.990 --> 00:11:03.700
Nobunaga is so simple, 
she's moving just as anticipated.

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:12.940
A wolf?

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:26.410
Thank you so much, your holiness.

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:31.870
N-Not at all. I'm sorry I can do no more.

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:33.710
Buddha save us...

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:48.130
Akerin, what's that?

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:51.310
<b>Hot Springs</b>

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:51.310
There's a hot spring.

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:52.790
A hot spring!

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:54.460
A hot spring, my lord!

00:11:54.460 --> 00:11:55.740
An outdoor bath!

00:11:55.740 --> 00:11:57.780
Let's all take a bath together!

00:11:57.780 --> 00:11:59.690
A bath, huh?

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:12.210
Didn't that priestess seem a bit scared of us?

00:12:12.900 --> 00:12:15.910
Those rumors have probably reached here, too.

00:12:15.910 --> 00:12:18.790
Who knows what story she's heard.

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:20.180
Huh, Mitsuhide?

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:28.810
I can't see...

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:32.020
What a view!

00:12:32.510 --> 00:12:34.780
Don't slip while you're having fun.

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:36.810
Here I go!

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:37.580
Huh?

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:39.820
Hideyoshi Jump!

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:48.270
Hey! What are you doing?

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:51.980
My lord?

00:12:51.980 --> 00:12:53.460
What's wrong, Mitsuhide?

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:54.830
In the bath too long already?

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:19.350
She screwed around too much in the bath.

00:13:19.350 --> 00:13:22.730
It was a hard walk for Hideyoshi.

00:13:22.730 --> 00:13:24.490
Her exhaustion caught up with her.

00:13:27.460 --> 00:13:29.140
It's fine.

00:13:29.140 --> 00:13:31.620
One dose of cold medicine, 
and I'll be back on my feet.

00:13:32.070 --> 00:13:33.320
Cold medicine?

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:34.250
What's that?

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:36.490
Oh, come on, Akerin.

00:13:36.490 --> 00:13:39.100
You know, cold medicine...

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:41.800
That's right... There's no medicine.

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:43.980
My lord,

00:13:43.980 --> 00:13:46.670
let's leave Hideyoshi in care 
of the priestesses here,

00:13:46.670 --> 00:13:48.190
and continue,

00:13:48.190 --> 00:13:51.060
just the two of us.

00:13:51.780 --> 00:13:53.100
Yeah.

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:56.450
Please don't leave me...

00:13:56.450 --> 00:13:57.770
Don't be stupid.

00:13:57.770 --> 00:13:59.900
You can't travel like this!

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:03.050
But...

00:14:03.050 --> 00:14:05.950
Then, let's wait a night and see.

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:08.280
Take this, Hideyoshi.

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:11.600
What is this?

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:14.030
A secret medicine, passed down 
for generations within the Oda clan.

00:14:14.030 --> 00:14:16.490
Medicine?

00:14:16.490 --> 00:14:17.210
Yes.

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:21.620
So you do have medicine. Good...

00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:34.520
What is this medicine?

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:38.310
I believe they take dried 
horse manure and boil it.

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:39.790
And then what...

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:40.860
Horse manure?

00:14:40.860 --> 00:14:42.820
Charred slugs and worms, don't you think?

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:45.620
Slugs and worms?

00:14:45.620 --> 00:14:48.370
Oh, that's right!

00:14:48.370 --> 00:14:49.080
They say,

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:50.860
the more bitter the medicine, the better it is.

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:53.140
Hey, Hideyoshi?

00:14:53.140 --> 00:14:55.330
What's wrong, Hideyoshi?

00:15:08.270 --> 00:15:09.950
How strange...

00:15:09.950 --> 00:15:12.530
Her fever is worsening, not improving.

00:15:12.530 --> 00:15:13.850
My lord...

00:15:14.820 --> 00:15:19.230
In this era, how long do people usually live?

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:20.630
Live?

00:15:22.090 --> 00:15:25.400
People are starting to live longer.

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:28.490
Fifty years, I'd say.

00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:32.950
Fifty years... That's all...

00:15:32.950 --> 00:15:36.580
But I don't think I'll last that long.

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:38.880
Snap out of it, Hideyoshi.

00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:40.990
They say that illness comes from the spirit.

00:15:41.470 --> 00:15:44.490
Your energy is your one good quality.

00:15:44.490 --> 00:15:46.710
If you talk like that, you won't get well.

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:48.760
My lord...

00:15:49.330 --> 00:15:50.960
Rest well.

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:53.410
I'll stay with you tonight.

00:15:53.410 --> 00:15:54.780
Yes...

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:59.270
Mitsuhide... You rest, too.

00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:01.260
My lord?

00:16:01.260 --> 00:16:02.920
I'll do this myself.

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:03.770
But...

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:07.110
I can't have you getting sick, as well.

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:12.620
I'll go get some hot water.

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:20.450
Nobunaga-sama, may I?

00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:28.670
I've never seen a pill like this.

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:34.460
A samurai came, asking directions.

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:37.590
When I explained that your companion was ill,

00:16:37.590 --> 00:16:41.040
she said she had some good medicine

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:45.210
from overseas, and gave this to us.

00:16:45.240 --> 00:16:48.920
But something from overseas would be expensive.

00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:50.360
I must thank her.

00:16:50.970 --> 00:16:54.990
She said it was as thanks, for telling her the way.

00:16:55.470 --> 00:16:57.400
She's already gone?

00:16:57.400 --> 00:16:58.550
Yes.

00:16:59.650 --> 00:17:01.940
What a strange person.

00:17:01.940 --> 00:17:07.080
But the rumors I'd heard were very wrong.

00:17:07.590 --> 00:17:08.910
I'd heard you were

00:17:08.910 --> 00:17:13.230
a terrifying woman, who ate the flesh of babies.

00:17:13.230 --> 00:17:15.940
I was so mistaken.

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:20.530
There are some things that must be told, 
or someone will never know.

00:17:20.530 --> 00:17:23.360
And there are some things someone 
will never know, even if they're told.

00:17:23.360 --> 00:17:24.100
Thus...

00:17:24.550 --> 00:17:26.100
This world is interesting.

00:17:26.950 --> 00:17:28.590
Enjoy your evening.

00:17:32.920 --> 00:17:34.030
My lord...

00:17:34.750 --> 00:17:35.650
What's wrong, Hideyoshi?

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:38.660
Don't leave me, my lord...

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:40.910
Oh, she's talking in her sleep.

00:17:42.780 --> 00:17:46.370
I don't want to be left alone.

00:17:48.470 --> 00:17:51.880
Hideyoshi... Hideyoshi, wake up.

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:53.880
Take this medicine.

00:17:57.450 --> 00:17:58.410
Take it.

00:17:58.410 --> 00:17:59.830
Take it, Hideyoshi!

00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:13.900
My lord, I brought some water...

00:18:29.050 --> 00:18:30.460
My lord.

00:18:31.260 --> 00:18:34.300
Why did you kiss me...

00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:36.400
It's OK.

00:18:36.400 --> 00:18:38.050
It's OK, Hideyoshi.

00:18:55.240 --> 00:18:58.490
She's such a difficult student.

00:19:11.390 --> 00:19:12.670
You're back, Hideyoshi?

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:15.250
Good morning.

00:19:19.060 --> 00:19:20.790
Your fever's gone down.

00:19:20.790 --> 00:19:24.430
It looks like that overseas medicine worked.

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:26.500
My lord?

00:19:26.500 --> 00:19:29.490
Did you watch over me all night?

00:19:30.430 --> 00:19:31.850
Don't worry about it.

00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:34.320
It was just like being on a battlefield.

00:19:34.930 --> 00:19:36.320
My lord...

00:19:37.410 --> 00:19:40.740
Good! Maybe that's why...

00:19:41.400 --> 00:19:45.690
I think it was the fever, but I had a dream.

00:19:47.090 --> 00:19:48.550
What kind of dream?

00:19:48.550 --> 00:19:50.340
Um, well...

00:19:50.710 --> 00:19:54.500
You kissed me...

00:19:54.910 --> 00:19:57.800
Kiss? What's a kiss?

00:19:58.710 --> 00:20:02.970
Oh, right... Um, in other words...

00:20:03.830 --> 00:20:08.010
You put your lips together like this.

00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:11.410
You... You know!

00:20:11.410 --> 00:20:13.110
D-Don't be stupid!

00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:15.770
I wouldn't do that!

00:20:15.770 --> 00:20:18.860
Oh, yeah. That's right.

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:35.670
My lord, we're nearly there.

00:20:37.510 --> 00:20:39.790
Is something on my face?

00:20:39.790 --> 00:20:41.330
Your eyes are red.

00:20:41.330 --> 00:20:43.030
Were you unable to sleep?

00:20:43.030 --> 00:20:44.320
No...

00:20:44.900 --> 00:20:48.810
I guess the journey is catching up to me, as well.

00:20:49.490 --> 00:20:50.440
I see.

00:20:50.440 --> 00:20:52.430
Take care of yourself.

00:20:53.220 --> 00:20:53.940
Yes.

00:20:56.470 --> 00:21:00.670
I wonder if I'll be able to make it in this world...

00:21:01.270 --> 00:21:03.120
Hideyoshi, look at that!

00:21:07.290 --> 00:21:08.520
That's...

00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:10.290
The sea!

00:21:10.650 --> 00:21:11.810
The sea!

00:21:11.810 --> 00:21:13.410
Then, we're in Saigoku!

00:21:13.800 --> 00:21:14.540
Yes.

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:17.420
Yay! We made it.

00:21:18.180 --> 00:21:19.730
Her moods change so quickly.

00:21:19.730 --> 00:21:21.260
She's like a child.

00:21:23.220 --> 00:21:26.760
<i>My emotions aren't reaching her.</i>

00:21:27.510 --> 00:21:30.560
Come on! Come on, my lord!

00:21:34.550 --> 00:21:37.270
That's Oda Nobunaga and her two companions.

00:21:37.830 --> 00:21:39.120
What do we do?

00:21:39.120 --> 00:21:41.030
We needn't let them into Saigoku.

00:21:41.440 --> 00:21:43.070
Want to just take 'em out?

00:21:43.550 --> 00:21:44.870
Wait.

00:21:44.870 --> 00:21:46.830
They're guests.

00:21:46.830 --> 00:21:49.660
We should take care of them properly.

00:21:50.210 --> 00:21:53.040
Yes. Properly...

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:28.760
<b>Hideyoshino 
Hidaka Rina</b>

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:52.360
<b>Sengoku Otome Style Preview</b>

00:23:25.470 --> 00:23:28.430
Sensei, why call me to the teacher's room again?

00:23:28.870 --> 00:23:32.520
I wanted your advice on our field trip, Hide-san.

00:23:28.970 --> 00:23:32.850
<b>Date-Sensei 
Hirata Yuka</b>

00:23:32.520 --> 00:23:33.090
Yes.

00:23:33.090 --> 00:23:35.940
This year, we're planning to go to Saigoku.

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:42.730
<b>Field 
Trip</b>

00:23:35.940 --> 00:23:39.290
As a student, is there anywhere you'd like to visit?

00:23:39.290 --> 00:23:40.080
Let me see...

00:23:40.080 --> 00:23:41.590
Wait a second.

00:23:42.330 --> 00:23:43.190
Is that a globe?

00:23:43.190 --> 00:23:44.150
Yes.

00:23:44.150 --> 00:23:44.860
A globe?

00:23:44.860 --> 00:23:48.190
Yes, let's see... Aikoku... Sugoku...

00:23:48.190 --> 00:23:49.580
How about Kyuushuu?

00:23:49.580 --> 00:23:50.330
Makes sense.

00:23:50.710 --> 00:23:52.410
And I don't know much about it, but...

00:23:52.410 --> 00:23:54.560
Watch next time, OK?

00:23:52.410 --> 00:23:58.560
Preview

00:23:52.410 --> 00:23:58.560
Saigoku Maiden
